1.1.text:
Article 10

Prevention of acts of violence against women as referred to in Article 6 paragraph (2) letter a, the Regional Government undertakes the following efforts:

a. conducting outreach and socialization regarding matters concerning violence against women;
b. conducting socialization on women's rights;
c. seeking to improve education for women;
d. opening skills courses for women to support family economic needs;
e. creating employment opportunities for women;
f. providing outreach to immediately report to local authorities if violence against women occurs;
g. empowering social community organizations and women's organizations to increase knowledge and women's insight;
h. establishing Women's Protection Complaint Posts; and i. forming networks in efforts to prevent violence.

Article 3

This Regional Regulation aims to:

a. ensure the fulfillment of women's rights so they can live and participate optimally in accordance with human dignity and worth;
b. prevent all forms of Violence against Women;
c. provide protection and a sense of security for women victims of violence and discrimination;
d. ensure the implementation of policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women by the region systematically, comprehensively, continuously, and in an integrated manner;
e. increase the commitment of the Regional Government in implementing policies, programs and activities for the protection of women; and
f. encourage institutions that handle the duties and functions of women's empowerment in the Regional Government and community institutions in the region to improve performance in efforts to protect women.

Article 4

The scope of this Regional Regulation includes:

a. rights of women victims of violence;
b. authority of the Regional Government;
c. planning;
d. Implementation ...

REGENT OF EAST KUTAI

d. implementation;

e. monitoring and evaluation;

f. reporting;

g. guidance and supervision;

h. community participation; and

i. funding.

Article 16

(1) SPM in the field of integrated services for women and children victims of violence aims to ensure that Female Victims of violence receive the minimum services needed.

(2) SPM in the field of integrated services for Female Victims of violence includes services:

a. handling of complaints/reports of Victims of Violence Against Women;
b. health services for female victims of violence; c. social rehabilitation for female victims of violence;
d. enforcement and Legal Aid for female victims of violence;
e. Repatriation and Social Reintegration for female victims of violence; and
f. in the event that a Female Victim of Violence experiences trauma or illness that endangers herself as a result of acts of violence so as to require immediate assistance, the Regional Government is obliged to provide first aid no later than 7 (seven) days after the complaint is filed.

Article 5

Every female victim of violence has the right:

a. to be respected for her dignity and worth as a human being;
b. to obtain protection from family, community, Regional Government and/or other parties either temporarily or based on the determination of a protection order from the court;
c. to recovery of physical, psychological and sexual health in accordance with the suffering experienced by Female Victims of Violence;
d. to special handling related to the confidentiality of Female Victims of Violence;
e. to assistance by social workers and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
f. to spiritual guidance services; and
g. to determine her own decisions.

CHAPTER III ...

REGENT OF EAST KUTAI

Article 25

(1) In organizing the Protection of Women, the community may: a. establish family partners at the sub-district/village level;

b. establish women's protection units within community organizations;

c. conduct independent socialization of Women's rights;

d. provide first aid to Women Victims of Violence;

e. report to the competent authority if violence against Women occurs in their environment.

f. prevent the occurrence of acts of violence against women.

g. provide information and/or report acts of violence against women to the competent authorities; and

h. forms ...

REGENT OF KUTAI TIMUR

h. forms and roles of the community are carried out responsibly in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

(2) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) includes: a. Individuals;

b. social community institutions;

c. non-governmental organizations;

d. educational institutions;

e. religious institutions;

f. private sector; and

g. mass media.

